362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (M1 Instability: Gemma 3 27B shows a high positive drift \(+17.6 pp\) under Prompt Hardening. This means it becomes significantly more vulnerable in longer conversations as the prompt context "dilutes" the safety instructions.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (The deep negative bars for Kimi K2 \(-39.2 pp\) and Qwen3 \(-24.3 pp\) under M3. M3 gets more effective over time because the more turns an attacker takes, the more "semantic signal" M3 accumulates to trigger a block.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
